WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.659 --> 00:00:06.100
Revenge might be a dish best served cold,
but these films all delivered red-hot justice.

00:00:06.100 --> 00:00:10.410
Whether it was an entire film's worth of elaborate
plotting and execution or a single moment

00:00:10.410 --> 00:00:14.600
of sweet revenge, here are some of the greatest
acts of revenge in movies ever.

00:00:14.600 --> 00:00:16.030
The Gift

00:00:16.030 --> 00:00:21.050
Joel Edgerton made his big-screen directorial
debut with 2015's The Gift, where he plays

00:00:21.050 --> 00:00:25.460
Gordo, a seemingly sad sack who runs into
an old high school acquaintance named Simon,

00:00:25.460 --> 00:00:27.070
played by Jason Bateman.

00:00:27.070 --> 00:00:31.080
Gordo turns into something of an unwanted
shadow for the man and his wife Robyn, but

00:00:31.080 --> 00:00:34.480
eventually, Gordo's kookiness becomes more
worrisome than weird.

00:00:34.480 --> 00:00:39.360
As Simon’s secrets come to light, Gordo
steps up his psyche-unraveling campaign of

00:00:39.360 --> 00:00:43.789
terror, including sending Simon disturbing
footage of his wife being drugged by Gordo

00:00:43.789 --> 00:00:45.920
nine months before the birth of her baby.

00:00:45.920 --> 00:00:51.160
In retaliation for a casual act of cruelty
that caused Gordo unfathomable pain, he makes

00:00:51.160 --> 00:00:54.219
Simon's question whether or not his child
is actually even his.

00:00:54.219 --> 00:00:57.040
Now that's what you call a mind game.

00:00:57.040 --> 00:00:58.670
The Help

00:00:58.670 --> 00:01:02.510
The Help from 2011 is set in the middle of
Mississippi during the civil rights movement.

00:01:02.510 --> 00:01:07.360
Octavia Spencer plays Minny, the long-suffering
maid to the horrible Hilly, a self-declared

00:01:07.360 --> 00:01:12.720
moral authority who leads the community charge
to segregate in-home bathrooms.

00:01:12.720 --> 00:01:17.290
Minny is fired for using the guest restroom
rather than brave a storm to access the outhouse

00:01:17.290 --> 00:01:21.880
facilities, but she makes Hilly eat her words
by cooking her a chocolate pie that contains

00:01:21.880 --> 00:01:27.900
a new special ingredient.

00:01:27.900 --> 00:01:32.960
Minny's...well...poop.

00:01:32.960 --> 00:01:37.640
It sounds foul, but it's actually quite a
delicious moment to watch as Hilly's brain

00:01:37.640 --> 00:01:41.970
catches up with her ears and understands what
she's just been told about the dessert she's

00:01:41.970 --> 00:01:44.920
still ravenously chowing down.

00:01:44.920 --> 00:01:46.560
Inglourious Basterds

00:01:46.560 --> 00:01:50.960
Vigilante justice is an essential element
in many of Quentin Tarantino's movies, but

00:01:50.960 --> 00:01:54.970
Inglourious Basterds tops Tarantino's catalogue
of excellent revenge moments.

00:01:54.970 --> 00:02:00.860
It’s a blood-soaked take on World War II-styled
vengeance against some of history's most reprehensible

00:02:00.860 --> 00:02:01.860
villains.

00:02:01.860 --> 00:02:04.300
From Shosanna's orchestrated torching of the
Führer…

00:02:04.300 --> 00:02:09.600
"Ha Ha Ha Ha Ha Ha Ha Ha Ha Ha Ha Ha Ha Ha
Ha"

00:02:09.600 --> 00:02:14.920
...to Donny "Bear Jew" Donowitz's merciless
beatdown of an remorseless SS officer, to

00:02:14.920 --> 00:02:20.950
Lt. Aldo Raine carving a swastika into Hans
Landa's forehead, Basterds dispenses justice

00:02:20.950 --> 00:02:25.640
in ways that only make the intense violence
that much more entertaining.

00:02:25.640 --> 00:02:26.640
Wanted

00:02:26.640 --> 00:02:31.320
It’s a scene that makes Jerry Maguire's
office exit speech seem like a note with a

00:02:31.320 --> 00:02:33.500
smiley face left on the company fridge.

00:02:33.500 --> 00:02:37.910
In Wanted, Wesley politely announces his departure
from the corporate world…

00:02:37.910 --> 00:02:42.040
"Some loser gets his head blown off at the
Metropolitan."

00:02:42.040 --> 00:02:43.690
"SHUT THE F*%K UP!"

00:02:43.690 --> 00:02:47.680
...and heads for the exit with his ripped-out
computer keyboard in hand.

00:02:47.680 --> 00:02:52.170
His buddy and co-worker Barry, who's befuddled
by what Wesley's just said to their boss,

00:02:52.170 --> 00:02:56.090
goes for the high five and gets a QWERTY to
the face instead.

00:02:56.090 --> 00:03:00.060
Appropriate, since Barry had been sleeping
with Wesley’s girlfriend.

00:03:00.060 --> 00:03:04.350
Wesley doubles down in his vengeance by making
out with the badass beauty Fox, played by

00:03:04.350 --> 00:03:07.569
Angelina Jolie, right in front of her.

00:03:07.569 --> 00:03:08.850
Man on Fire

00:03:08.850 --> 00:03:13.960
In the 2004 action-drama Man on Fire, a retired
CIA operative named John Creasy, played by

00:03:13.960 --> 00:03:20.210
Denzel Washington, takes a gig as the bodyguard-slash-babysitter
of a nine-year-old girl named Pita, but comes

00:03:20.210 --> 00:03:24.000
to find that the job entails a lot more than
mere child's play.

00:03:24.000 --> 00:03:28.340
When Pita is kidnapped, Creasy gets to work
finding and systematically slaughtering her

00:03:28.340 --> 00:03:29.620
captors.

00:03:29.620 --> 00:03:34.600
In the movie’s most memorable revenge scene,
Creasy ties a potential kidnapper down to

00:03:34.600 --> 00:03:36.970
a car and, well…

00:03:36.970 --> 00:03:39.520
"C4, highly explosive.

00:03:39.520 --> 00:03:42.060
You put them all together and you got a bomb.

00:03:42.060 --> 00:03:44.280
Not very sophisticated but very powerful.

00:03:44.280 --> 00:03:49.120
That's what you have in your ass right now."

00:03:49.120 --> 00:03:53.120
The perp spills the beans, but Creasy is unforgiving.

00:03:53.120 --> 00:03:55.680
Never mess with Denzel.

00:03:55.680 --> 00:03:57.590
Road to Perdition

00:03:57.590 --> 00:04:02.580
This Depression-era drama, Road to Perdition,
follows Mafia enforcer Michael Sullivan, played

00:04:02.580 --> 00:04:07.420
by Tom Hanks, seeking justice for his wife
and child, who were murdered by his mentor’s

00:04:07.420 --> 00:04:10.160
son, Connor, played by Daniel Craig.

00:04:10.160 --> 00:04:14.240
With his surviving son in tow, Sullivan works
his way through the deadly crime syndicate

00:04:14.240 --> 00:04:16.500
to find Connor and make him pay.

00:04:16.500 --> 00:04:20.820
The journey is filled with treachery and devastation,
but in the end, the parties who deserve it

00:04:20.820 --> 00:04:26.270
get theirs—even Sullivan, whose son watches
him pay the ultimate sacrifice for his life

00:04:26.270 --> 00:04:27.960
of violence.

00:04:27.960 --> 00:04:29.940
The Shawshank Redemption

00:04:29.940 --> 00:04:33.950
When the word “redemption” is in the title,
you can probably be sure that things will

00:04:33.950 --> 00:04:38.790
turn around by the end of the movie, and the
40-year saga of Andy Dufresne's false imprisonment

00:04:38.790 --> 00:04:40.160
is no exception.

00:04:40.160 --> 00:04:44.630
While the man who actually committed the murders
for which Andy is convicted is eventually

00:04:44.630 --> 00:04:47.480
imprisoned, he isn't the one who earns Andy's
true wrath.

00:04:47.480 --> 00:04:52.190
Instead, it’s Shawshank’s Warden Norton,
who has the opportunity to free Andy after

00:04:52.190 --> 00:04:54.980
evidence of his wrongful imprisonment comes
to light.

00:04:54.980 --> 00:05:00.180
Instead of doing so, Norton punishes Andy
further—all the while, relying on Andy to

00:05:00.180 --> 00:05:04.080
cook his books so he can launder money under
the name “Randall Stephens”.

00:05:04.080 --> 00:05:08.810
After Andy escapes to freedom, he adopts the
Randall Stephens alias to siphon off the warden’s

00:05:08.810 --> 00:05:13.550
ill-gotten loot, and turns evidence of Norton's
crimes over to the feds, leaving the warden

00:05:13.550 --> 00:05:16.970
no choice but to off himself in his own office.

00:05:16.970 --> 00:05:17.970
John Wick

00:05:17.970 --> 00:05:24.220
A grieving widower receives a strange present
one day: an adorable little puppy, the final

00:05:24.220 --> 00:05:29.000
gift from his dead wife, and a chance for
him to start over and appreciate life despite

00:05:29.000 --> 00:05:30.290
his loss.

00:05:30.290 --> 00:05:34.190
That's how 2014's John Wick, starring Keanu
Reeves starts out.

00:05:34.190 --> 00:05:38.340
It doesn't take long, however, for the son
of a Russian mob boss to break into Wick's

00:05:38.340 --> 00:05:43.270
house, kill his puppy, and beat him to a pulp
— all so he can steal his car.

00:05:43.270 --> 00:05:44.270
Big mistake.

00:05:44.270 --> 00:05:49.699
"Cause he stole John Wicks car sir, and ah,
killed his dog."

00:05:55.300 --> 00:05:55.800
"oh"

00:05:57.229 --> 00:06:01.160
That's when the viewers find out who John
Wick really is: one of the most fearsome and

00:06:01.160 --> 00:06:03.880
effective hitmen to ever retire from the business.

00:06:03.880 --> 00:06:09.280
"People keep asking if I'm back and I haven't
really had an answer.

00:06:09.280 --> 00:06:12.870
But now, yeah, I'm thinking I'm back."

00:06:12.870 --> 00:06:18.040
What follows is one of the best, most action-packed
revenge movies in recent history, featuring

00:06:18.040 --> 00:06:21.650
Wick taking out the Russian mob piece by piece.

00:06:21.650 --> 00:06:25.860
When Wick finally catches up to the creep
who killed his dog, he takes out his bodyguards

00:06:25.860 --> 00:06:31.000
with a sniper rifle, blows up his getaway
cars, and shoots him in the guts, all before

00:06:31.000 --> 00:06:33.630
finally putting a bullet in his head while
he's mid-sentence.

00:06:33.630 --> 00:06:38.010
"это был просто"

00:06:38.010 --> 00:06:39.270
Thanks for watching!

00:06:39.270 --> 00:06:42.960
Subscribe to our YouTube channel to watch
more videos like the one you just saw.

00:06:42.960 --> 00:06:46.070
And leave us a comment to let us know which
revenge scenes are your favorite...

